  11→```
  12→
  13→Displacing points along their normals automatically updates the normal vectors when smooth shading is applied.
  14→
  15→### Vector Addition Basics
  16→
  17→```vex
  18→vector a = chv('a');
  19→vector b = chv('b');
  20→@P = a+b;
  21→```
  22→
  23→Demonstrates basic vector addition by creating two vector parameters and adding them together to set the point position.
  24→
  25→### Vector Addition Basics
  26→
  27→```vex
  28→vector a = chv('a');
  29→vector b = chv('b');
  30→@N = a + b;
  31→```
  32→
  33→Demonstrates basic vector addition by creating two vector parameters and adding them together, storing the result in the normal attribute.
  34→
  35→### Vector Addition Basics
  36→
  37→```vex
  38→vector a = chv('a');
  39→vector b = chv('b');
  40→@P = a + b;
  41→```
  42→
  43→Demonstrates basic vector addition by reading two vector parameters from channel references and setting the point position to their sum.
  44→
  45→### Adding Vector to Position
  46→
  47→```vex
  48→vector a = chv('a');
  49→@P += a;
  50→```
  51→
  52→Reads a vector parameter from a UI channel and adds it to the point position.
  53→
  54→### Setting Normals with Channel Reference
  55→
  56→```vex
  57→@N = chf('scale');
  58→```
  59→
  60→Sets the normal vector (@N) to a uniform scalar value controlled by a channel parameter named 'scale'.
  61→
  62→### Scaling Normals with Channel Reference
  63→
  64→```vex
  65→@N *= ch('scale');
  66→```
  67→
  68→Multiplies the normal vector by a channel parameter named 'scale', allowing interactive control over normal magnitude for effects like explosions or directional displacement.
  69→
  70→### Scaling Normals with Channel
  71→
  72→```vex
  73→v@N * ch('scale');
  74→```
  75→
  76→Multiplies the normal vector by a channel parameter value, demonstrating vector multiplication with scalar values from channel references.
  77→
  78→### Multiplication with Channel Reference
  79→
  80→```vex
  81→@P *= ch('scale');
  82→```
  83→
  84→Multiplies the position of each point by a channel parameter named 'scale', effectively scaling the geometry uniformly.
  85→
  86→### Vector Scaling with Parameters
  87→
  88→```vex
  89→*= ch('scale');
  90→```
  91→
  92→Uses the compound assignment operator to scale a vector attribute by a channel parameter value.
  93→
  94→### Vector-Vector Multiplication with chv()
  95→
